<urn:atm:triage:finding/EQ-008>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "EQ-008" ;
  triage:title "atm task assign by a non-assigner returns success (exit 0, task_id) but silently no-ops instead of reassigning or refusing" ;
  triage:description "fenix, 2026-09-14, relayed from the AT10 agent's report in colima run 20260914T035038469557Z (/opt/data/results/prompt-AT10.json in the container). `atm task assign <other> --task-id <existing task>`, run by an identity that is NOT the task's current assigner (fx-at10-beta), returns {\"task_id\":...} with exit 0 -- but changes nothing: `atm task events <id> --all --json` is byte-identical before and after the call, and the task's assignee field is unchanged. The daemon appears to only record a plain task-tagged message rather than actually performing (or refusing) the reassignment. The observable result is a success response for a reassignment that did not happen, rather than an explicit refusal/error indicating the caller lacks assigner authority. atm version 1.5.17. IMPORTANT CAVEAT (fenix, explicit): this evidence is agent-observed through the public CLI inside the colima container (AT10's own prompt/report), fenix has NOT independently reproduced it by hand outside that run. Filed for verification, not as a confirmed defect -- the first triage/dispatch step should be a manual repro (assign a task, have a non-assigner identity attempt `atm task assign` on it, diff `atm task events --all --json` before/after) before any fix is written." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-bb" ;
  triage:triageMode "evidence_verification" ;
  triage:category "correctness" ;
  triage:severity "important" ;
  triage:source "fenix, relayed from AT10 agent report, colima run 20260914T035038469557Z, 2026-09-14 (ATM message 01M2F2K5JQ2DJTY320BFX9ZVZW) -- not independently reproduced by fenix" ;
  triage:repeatable false ;
  triage:sweepScope "atm task assign / atm-daemon task-reassignment authorization path: manual repro first (non-assigner identity calling `atm task assign <other> --task-id <existing>`, diff `atm task events <id> --all --json` before/after); if reproduced, fix to either perform the reassignment when authorized or return a non-zero exit / explicit refusal when the caller is not the current assigner" ;
  triage:status "open" ;
  triage:dispatchReady true ;
  triage:triagedAt "2026-09-14T00:00:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:foundIn triage:BB8 ;
  triage:foundAt "2026-09-14T00:00:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/EQ-008/1> ;
  triage:triageRecordVersion "1" .

